---
import BaseHead from "../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../../consts";

const pageTitle = "Mutation Testing Resources";
const pageDescription =
    "A curated selection of mutation testing tools, papers, and talks – with extra focus on Rust and Solidity.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <BaseHead
            title={`${pageTitle} | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
            description={pageDescription || SITE_DESCRIPTION}
        />
    </head>
    <body>
        <Header />
        <main>
            <section class="hero">
                <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
                <p class="tagline">
                    A hand-picked “best of” mutation testing – focused on
                    high-signal tools and learning resources rather than an
                    exhaustive list.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This page is curated by Mutorium Labs and built on top of
                    the community-maintained{" "}
                    <a
                        href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noreferrer"
                    >
                        Awesome Mutation Testing
                    </a>{" "}
                    list. If you want everything, go there. If you want a guided
                    path, start here.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>Core introductions</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://testing.googleblog.com/2021/04/mutation-testing.html"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Mutation Testing (Google Testing Blog, 2021)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – short, practical explanation of why a large engineering
                        org uses mutation testing and what it changes in day-to-day
                        development.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://www.thegreenreport.blog/articles/the-power-of-mutation-testing/the-power-of-mutation-testing.html"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            The Power of Mutation Testing (2024)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – modern, readable overview of concepts and benefits.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing#publications"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Publications section of Awesome Mutation Testing
                        </a>{" "}
                        – if you want the full academic background, start here.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>Rust</h2>
                <p>
                    Our main language focus. These are the tools we consider
                    most relevant if you write or study Rust code.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/sourcefrog/cargo-mutants"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            cargo-mutants
                        </a>{" "}
                        – source-level mutation testing for Rust. Mutates your code
                        and re-runs <code>cargo test</code>. Great reference for
                        CLI design, operator choices, and JSON outputs.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/llogiq/mutagen"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            mutagen
                        </a>{" "}
                        – experimental mutation testing for Rust using attributes.
                        Interesting for exploring alternative operator and integration
                        strategies.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing#rust"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Rust section in Awesome Mutation Testing
                        </a>{" "}
                        – for more context and related links.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>Solidity &amp; smart contracts</h2>
                <p>
                    Smart contracts are a natural fit for mutation testing:
                    small programs, high stakes. These are the key tools to
                    know.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/Certora/gambit"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Certora/gambit
                        </a>{" "}
                        – a mutation system for Solidity used to evaluate both tests
                        and formal verification specifications.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/RareSkills/vertigo-rs"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            RareSkills/vertigo-rs
                        </a>{" "}
                        – actively maintained Rust implementation of Vertigo with
                        Foundry support. Mutates contracts and runs{" "}
                        <code>forge test</code> to produce a mutation score.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/JoranHonig/vertigo"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            JoranHonig/vertigo
                        </a>{" "}
                        – original Vertigo tool for mutation testing of smart contracts.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://rareskills.io/post/solidity-mutation-testing"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Solidity Mutation Testing (RareSkills)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – practical overview of how Solidity mutation tools work
                        and where they fit into a security workflow.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>Key papers (short list)</h2>
                <p>
                    For a deeper understanding, these are good entry points from
                    the much longer bibliography in Awesome Mutation Testing.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        A general survey such as{" "}
                        <em
                            >Mutation Testing Advances: An Analysis and Survey</em
                        >{" "}
                        – covers core ideas, operators, and research directions.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        An empirical study like{" "}
                        <em
                            >Are Mutants a Valid Substitute for Real Faults in
                            Software Testing?</em
                        > – addresses how well mutants approximate real bugs.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        A smart-contract–focused work such as{" "}
                        <em
                            >RegularMutator: A Mutation Testing Tool for
                            Solidity Smart Contracts</em
                        > – shows how mutation operators look in the Solidity domain.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        For more, see the{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing#publications"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Publications
                        </a>{" "}
                        section and follow the citation chains.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>Talks &amp; videos</h2>
                <p>
                    If you prefer to see mutation testing in action, these are
                    good starting talks.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LoFJajoJQ2g"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            GOTO 2019 – Making Mutants Work for You (Henry
                            Coles)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – live demos and a clear explanation of why mutation testing
                        improves test suites.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jwB3Nn4hR1o"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            GOTO 2015 – Mutation Testing in Python (Austin
                            Bingham)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – language-specific, but great for understanding general
                        concepts and tooling.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        More links are under{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing#blogsposts"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Blogs/Posts
                        </a>{" "}
                        and{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/theofidry/awesome-mutation-testing#videos"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            Videos
                        </a>{" "}
                        in the Awesome list.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="section">
                <h2>From Mutorium Labs</h2>
                <p>
                    These are our own resources that build on the tools and
                    papers above, especially in the context of Web3 and ZK.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="/blog/what-is-mutation-testing/">
                            What Is Mutation Testing? A Practical Introduction
                        </a>{" "}
                        – our long-form explanation of the concept, aimed at practitioners.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="/blog/swiss-cheese-model-of-web3/">
                            Swiss Cheese Model of Web3 Security
                        </a>{" "}
                        – how mutation testing fits into a layered defence model
                        for smart contracts and ZK systems.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="/book/">
                            The Mutorium Labs Book of Mutation Testing
                        </a>{" "}
                        – a living, programmer-focused book; chapters are published
                        as blog posts first.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/mutorium/noir-metrics"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noreferrer"
                        >
                            noir-metrics (GitHub)
                        </a>{" "}
                        – metrics for Noir/Nargo projects, forming the basis for
                        future coverage and mutation testing work on ZK circuits.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </main>
        <Footer />
    </body>
</html>
